-- title:
--   Level raising by ℓ is finite and flat on j-charts
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M \neq 0$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and a discrete valuation domain $A$ which is an $L$-algebra with $L$ as its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$. Fix further a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid M p$. Let $K_M$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ obtained as the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image along $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion field of $\Gamma_1(M)$, and let $K_N$ be the corresponding field for $\Gamma_1(M\ell)$; both are equipped with $A$-algebra structures compatible with $A \to L$. Let $j_M \in K_M$ and $j_N \in K_N$ be elements whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNumQ}$ of the modular invariant, each assumed nonzero, and assume $K_M \le K_N$ inside $L((q))$. Write $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,F\,j$ for the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $A[j]$, i.e. the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $F$. Given an $A$-algebra homomorphism $\iota_M$ from $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K_M\,j_M$ to $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K_N\,j_N$ that is the identity on underlying Laurent series, the conclusion is that the underlying ring homomorphism of $\iota_M$ is both finite and flat.
--
--   This is the local statement, at the level of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model over $A$, that the degeneracy map from level $M\ell$ to level $M$ on $X_1$ is finite and flat away from the point at infinity. It feeds the corresponding finite-and-étale assertion for the same map, the starting point for the comparison of the two levels in the level-raising argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOne_finite_and_flat_chartAlgFin_levelRaise_x1.lean

